WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.635 line:0%
-Tyler, it is great to see you.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.303 line:0%
Thank you for being on the show.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.939 line:0%
I'm assuming you're in the --
You're at your studio?

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.774 line:0%
Is that where you are?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:12.512 line:0%
I'm in Sound Stage 5,
the Diahann Carroll Sound Stage.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.546 line:0%
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.780 line:0%
But, man, we got to get --

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.182 line:0%
Listen, we got to get
a vaccine or something.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:19.284 line:0%
This is -- Come on, come on.
Come on, man.

00:00:19.284 --> 00:00:20.686 line:0%
We have fun together.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:24.390 line:0%
We fly planes and race cars,
and how can we do that here?

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.227 line:0%
So, yeah, I love it.
-Please, let's just get one.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.929 line:0%
Just -- If anyone is listening,
come on, Tyler Perry wants one.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.163 line:0%
Let's go.
I mean, I've been asking.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.032 line:0%
-That's right. That's right.
-I've been asking.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.300 line:0%
-That's right.
-Please

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.069 line:0%
Madea is working on one,
but I don't think anybody

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.737 line:0%
wants to take it right away.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.307 line:0%
It's kind of like injecting
bleach into the body

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.476 line:0%
with, like, a light
and making sure it works.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:46.379 line:0%
That was her idea first, so...

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.481 line:0%
-How is the quarantine?

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.718 line:0%
Did you create, like, a bubble
of just everyone in your world?

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.086 line:0%
Or just you?

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:56.556 line:0%
-Yeah, I've got 377 people in
quarantine, starting --

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.924 line:0%
We just wrapped for a week.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:01.193 line:0%
So, we shoot a show for
two weeks, we go home a week,

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.462 line:0%
come back two more weeks.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.997 line:0%
So, we're getting ready to
start our final show.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.532 line:0%
It's a three-week stretch,
so everybody is home right now.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.901 line:0%
They start checking in tomorrow,
re-testing tomorrow,

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:09.936 line:0%
and we're gonna go from there.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.071 line:0%
It's like adult summer camp.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.572 line:0%
You know, I was telling them --
I was like,

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:16.208 line:0%
"Guys, listen, I know you're all
here and beautiful

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:17.476 line:0%
and young, single people.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.945 line:0%
I can protect you from COVID,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.479 line:0%
but I can't protect you
from the clap.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.014 line:0%
So, you know, it's all --

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:25.651 line:0%
You've got to handle
that for yourself.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.521 line:0%
-Yeah, come on.
-This is about a COVID-free.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.324 line:0%
-Yeah, "I can only do so much."
-Can't do that, can't do that.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.660 line:0%
-Are you maintaining the pace
that you're always doing

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.796 line:0%
or are things moving
a little slower?

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.598 line:0%
-No, no, no.
We haven't slowed down.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.200 line:0%
My crew -- I had to have
a smaller crew,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.936 line:0%
so our moves take longer,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.138 line:0%
but, no, we're
rockin' and rollin', man.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.840 line:0%
And we have movies in
the evening on the lawn.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.142 line:0%
We have four or five different
food trucks.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.678 line:0%
We have an alcohol truck.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:55.047 line:0%
It's really -- We're enjoying it
as we're working.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:56.749 line:0%
-Gosh, that is fantastic.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:01.053 line:0%
You got some news recently that
you're going to receive

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:05.024 line:0%
the Governors Award at
this year's Emmys ceremony.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.493 line:0%
What does that mean to you?
-Wouldn't you know it?

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.128 line:0%
They'd do it in a year where
everything is virtual?

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:13.565 line:0%
I said, "Listen --"
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:15.167 line:0%
I'm like, "I don't give a damn.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:18.304 line:0%
You tell me where it is, I'm
showing up in full hazmat suit.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.472 line:0%
I will be there,"

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.074 line:0%
'cause it's such
an incredible honor.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:24.177 line:0%
And to think that the governors

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.645 line:0%
would actually consider me
for this is beyond --

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:28.047 line:0%
I'm blown away by it.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.415 line:0%
-Well, you deserve
the recognition

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.984 line:0%
for everything you're doing.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:34.720 line:0%
But I've got to say,
during this pandemic,

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.589 line:0%
you've really been looking
out for others

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.923 line:0%
and helping people.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.327 line:0%
Even just your donations.
You're giving to individuals.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:45.798 line:0%
You cover grocery bills
for the elderly.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.501 line:0%
You help
local restaurant workers.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.537 line:0%
Why is it important for you
to give directly to the people?

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.674 line:0%
-Well, just look around
at how much direct

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:58.010 line:0%
anger and sadness and division,
and everybody is going --

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.979 line:0%
Everybody is grabbing a color
and running to a corner,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.247 line:0%
and nobody's coming together.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.015 line:0%
So I wanted to just be
out there doing things

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.350 line:0%
that inspire people,
'cause I feel like if I do it,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.321 line:0%
it will inspire other people to
stop so much of this

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.555 line:0%
division and come together,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.991 line:0%
because where change happens
is in the middle.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.793 line:0%
So every time I'm giving,
I'm hoping that

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.861 line:0%
I'm inspiring somebody
else to do the same.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.597 line:0%
-Yeah, you definitely inspire me
to do more,

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:19.732 line:0%
'cause I saw that
and I was like,

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.367 line:0%
"Oh, I'm just
going to get delivery

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.070 line:0%
even if I don't want delivery,
and I'll just tip the person."

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.604 line:0%
I go, "I'll just put it in
the freezer.

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:26.706 line:0%
I'm stocked."

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:30.342 line:0%
Just to keep people fed
and get money

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:31.744 line:0%
and get something moving.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.945 line:0%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.748 line:0%
-I also read a beautiful essay
that you wrote

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:40.653 line:0%
for "People" magazine in the
wake of George Floyd's murder.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:45.457 line:0%
It was very powerful and moving.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.327 line:0%
What is it like for you
to sit down and write that?

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.229 line:0%
Did you say,
"I have to do something,"

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.297 line:0%
or did somebody ask you to or...

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:56.435 line:0%
-No, that was hard.
I was so troubled by his death.

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:59.538 line:0%
And I -- When I started
to put pen to paper,

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:00.873 line:0%
I had a flood of emotion.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.074 line:0%
I was in tears by the time

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.509 line:0%
I got through
the first couple of sentences,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.345 line:0%
because I didn't realize how
much of it I had been carrying

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.447 line:0%
and how much of it for so long.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:13.152 line:0%
And what happened out of all
of that tragedy,

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.821 line:0%
seeing all races
galvanized together

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:18.458 line:0%
to stand up
against police brutality,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:23.028 line:0%
it was really moving and
inspiring on so many levels,

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.330 line:0%
so I was glad to see that,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.831 line:0%
'cause that's when
change happens.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.534 line:0%
Black and brown people are only
12% to 14% of the population,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.237 line:0%
so we need everyone
to make a change happen.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.872 line:0%
And to see us all
coming together,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.842 line:0%
that's what America is --
standing together as one,

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.345 line:0%
not being divided and pitted
against each other.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:43.649 line:0%
-Two months after writing it
now, where is your head at now?

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.251 line:0%
-Well, I've got to tell you,
I was really, really hopeful

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:48.053 line:0%
in the beginning, because
I thought,

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.188 line:0%
"Okay, everybody is galvanized.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.256 line:0%
This is gonna be great."

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.690 line:0%
But what I'm seeing now
troubles me,

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.695 line:0%
because it's being weaponized
in this political climate.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.864 line:0%
Black Lives Matter is being
pulled apart and ripped here.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:02.001 line:0%
And what I tell people about my
life and what I've done is,

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.537 line:0%
listen, two years ago,
when a white police officer

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.639 line:0%
was shot in the head
for trying to stop a shoplifter,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.673 line:0%
I reached out to his family

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.609 line:0%
to see what I can do
to help them.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.710 line:0%
And with George Floyd
and Rayshard Brooks

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.679 line:0%
and Secoriea,
this 8-year-old who was killed

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.447 line:0%
at a Wendy's restaurant,
I reached out to see

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:16.515 line:0%
what I could do to help.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:17.849 line:0%
It's not about race.

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:22.055 line:0%
It's about what you do and who
you are as a human being.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.056 line:0%
And humanity is
real for all of us.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:26.492 line:0%
So I was trying to make sure
that we all know

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.461 line:0%
that humanity comes
in all shades and sizes,

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:32.197 line:0%
and you have to treat people as
if they're human beings

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:33.833 line:0%
rather than as if
they're just --

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.669 line:0%
They're dismissing them because
of their race or whatever.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.571 line:0%
-Yeah, I think --
Yeah, we can do better,

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:43.208 line:0%
I think, was the big point that
I think was getting out there.

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.978 line:0%
I just hope that we keep
having these conversations

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.714 line:0%
until there is actual change,
and you go, "Yeah --"

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:51.083 line:0%
-That's the point, man --
having the conversation.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.385 line:0%
If everybody is going to
their corners

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.653 line:0%
and taking up arms,
nothing happens.

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:57.456 line:0%
We've got to come to the middle
and have hard conversations,

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.525 line:0%
uncomfortable conversations,
you know?

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.793 line:0%
That's what we need to do.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.228 line:0%
And I think as long as
we're doing that,

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:05.764 line:0%
we're going to see some great
things continue to move forward.

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:08.601 line:0%
-Let's talk about "Tyler Perry's
Madea's Farewell Play."

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.135 line:0%
We talked about this.
-Yes!

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.137 line:0%
-Oh! Just even doing the voice.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:16.576 line:0%
It's streaming on
BET+ starting August 27th.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.445 line:0%
How do you think Madea
would handle quarantine?

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.248 line:0%
-[ As Madea ] Well, baby,
I've been wearing my masks-s-s.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.549 line:0%
I've been wearing all
my masks-s-s-s.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.150 line:0%
Every time I go out,
I put on my masks-s-s-s.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.521 line:0%
I have one here and two here.
All my masks are all over.

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:33.626 line:0%
[ Normal voice ] She can't say
mask, so they're masks-s-s-s-s.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:36.528 line:0%
-I've got to be honest,
You've talked --

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.230 line:0%
I've had you on the show
so many times.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.633 line:0%
We've talked about
how these movies start with

00:06:41.633 --> 00:06:43.536 line:0%
plays and your fans.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.705 line:0%
It starts small
and just grows from there.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:49.508 line:0%
And I was always like, "I have
to go see you perform live,

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:50.910 line:0%
because I want to see
what it's like."

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.847 line:0%
I really -- So, you --
This is a staged play.

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:58.417 line:0%
This is a full-on play of
your final time playing her.

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:02.722 line:0%
But I had no idea.
It crushes. It is so fun.

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:03.756 line:0%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.790 line:0%
And that's what we need
right now.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:05.824 line:0%
This is what I tell people.

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:08.627 line:0%
Get BET+, sign up for it,
watch this play.

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:09.895 line:0%
It is so funny.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.797 line:0%
If you just want to laugh,
just have a good laugh

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.100 line:0%
with Madea and Brown
and Cora and Aunt Bam

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.101 line:0%
and all those characters
that you know --

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:19.071 line:0%
-Oh! Aunt Bam --
that's my favorite.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.639 line:0%
Cassi, yeah.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:23.575 line:0%
-Cassi Davis is
unbelievably talented,

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:25.511 line:0%
always scores for me.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.279 line:0%
Hooty-hoo
is all I'm going to say.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:29.515 line:0%
-Hooty-hoo. That's right.
That's right. That's right.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.150 line:0%
So, I tell you,
if you want to laugh,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.151 line:0%
with everything that's
going on in the country,

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:33.385 line:0%
just watch the play.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:34.620 line:0%
You know, over the years,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.922 line:0%
I've sold millions and millions
of these DVDs,

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:38.857 line:0%
and now you get to
stream it your house

00:07:38.857 --> 00:07:41.927 line:0%
just by signing up for BET+,
which I think is awesome.

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:45.998 line:0%
-I've got to ask you,
is it really the end of Madea?

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:48.901 line:0%
I mean, you'll never
play her again?

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.370 line:0%
-You know, I said
I was done with her

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.838 line:0%
unless she had something to say.

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.506 line:0%
Watching what's happening
in the country right now,

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:55.674 line:0%
I think she has
something to say.

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:56.909 line:0%
She may be running
for president.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:08:00.479 line:0%
We'll see.
-I loved it.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:03.049 line:0%
I will also say, again,
about the cast,

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:07.687 line:0%
not only are they funny, but,
gosh, they can really sing.

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:09.655 line:0%
-Yeah. Some of the
most incredible voices.

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.356 line:0%
That's why we have to use those
big, huge microphones

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:14.059 line:0%
on the forehead, because we blow
out the other little microphones

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:15.260 line:0%
that they use on Broadway.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.395 line:0%
-I mean, that --
-These microphones --

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:17.930 line:0%
-Yeah, these microphones
have to handle

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.032 line:0%
some really powerful voices.

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:24.469 line:0%
-I was just like, "Wow!
That was powerful."

00:08:24.469 --> 00:08:29.908 line:0%
And we got to see Madea do some
pretty cool moves at the end.

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:31.010 line:0%
-Yes, yes.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:34.380 line:0%
She went back
to her stripper days.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.648 line:0%
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:38.150 line:0%
-Bodacious? What was her ---

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.185 line:0%
-[ As Madea ] Bodacious, baby.
Bodacious Platinum.

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:43.455 line:0%
That was my name as a stripper,
Bodacious Platinum.

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:45.358 line:0%
-There's so many things
that made me laugh.

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:48.127 line:0%
It was -- The cast is fantastic.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:49.729 line:0%
And it really, really
made me laugh,

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:50.862 line:0%
and we all do need laughter.

00:08:50.862 --> 00:08:51.931 line:0%
We need entertainment.

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.799 line:0%
And so thanks
for everything you do.

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.968 line:0%
And, also, there's
a speech you say at the end

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:58.771 line:0%
of the performance that I think
everyone should stick around

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:00.472 line:0%
and just hear you talk about,

00:09:00.472 --> 00:09:04.743 line:0%
because it basically tells
everyone, "Hey, don't stop."

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:05.844 line:0%
-Yeah. Exactly right.

